  "answer": "In Q1 2026, citation reliability was \"the single most prominent complaint\" and the top customer pain point [NL-010#NL-010-S01]. The Q1 support audit found incorrect file links (42%), missing page numbers (28%), empty citations (18%), and broken links (12%) [NL-010#NL-010-S05], which caused enterprise customers such as BrightPath Healthcare to pause pilots and Northstar Financial to lose confidence [NL-010#NL-010-S05].\n\nIn Q2 2026, feedback trends improved significantly after the April 2026 fix. Overall NPS rose from 41 in Q1 to 44 in Q2, driven by the product update that \"addressed critical citation reliability issues\" [NL-011#NL-011-S01]. Citation-related complaints \"decreased significantly\" [NL-016#NL-016-S04]. Support tickets for citation accuracy declined from 72 in January, 79 in February, and 88 in March to 42 in April, 31 in May, and 24 in June [NL-011#NL-011-S05].\n\nHowever, citation reliability was not fully resolved: remaining tickets in May and June were \"almost entirely linked to scanned, image-only PDFs,\" where citation anchors are difficult to establish, and there is a minor lag in citation indexing during peak hours [NL-011#NL-011-S05]. Similarly, scanned/image-only PDFs continue to cause citation issues due to lack of advanced OCR [NL-016#NL-016-S04].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
